t  was I thought were quite quite  interesting for the mid 20th century  down there right right because today  that's kind of on point it's a trend for  sustainability reasons to reuse some  products that's right yeah and then  lastly I know you just launched a  competition an architecture competition  so talk a little bit about that  so we I've come to an agreement with  this major architectural award and they  heard me complain about you know the  lack of opportunity for for me to having  to have a museum that is permanent for  the collection right because I always  consider the collection to be public I  always consider myself to be an  administrator of a collection I never  say this art belongs to me because I  feel like you know whatever long my  lifespan is I really hope this life that  this this work lives for generations and  maybe hopefully centuries ahead and so I  my dream was to build a you know a  structure that houses the this  collection and so we just decided to  launch this competition it doesn't mean  I have the money to build the museum but  I wanted to get the public interested in  this idea and it's only been it's only  been launched recently but so far the  feedback has been very positive because  I'm calling on people to look at the  entire region and draw inspiration from  North Africa from the Levant from the  Gulf from Western from the entire region  when they propose an architectural  landmark that houses this collection is  there something that you particularly  would like to see incorporated into the  design let me would that be you know a  spoiler alert there's a spoiler alert  but the last glass the better okay cuz I  you know I also think of the environment  and I don't like the idea of these glass  houses that are being built in the Gulf  there's there's too much use of glass  and I'd like us to look back into what  we talked about a few minutes ago about  environmental consciousness about being  aware of the environment of these cities  at least you know this region's that we  inhabit and hopefully have a building  that's not just an architectural  landmark  but also you know a building that we can  look forward to in the future and say  this was a building that took the  environment into consideration right  well we will look forward to seeing the  outcome of that competition hopefully in  the near future thank you so much for  being here with us today thank you for  having me Marlon for more information  about Mr Al Qasimi please visit our  website at macmillan report yeah edu be  sure to join us again for another  episode of the Macmillan report made  possible through funding from the  Whitney and Betty Macmillan Center for  International and area studies at Yale  thank you very much thank you for having  me  you
 

